    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p81-q54-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p81-q54-a-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Show that the volume ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "V",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " of the box is given by",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p81-q54-a-formula",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "center",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "V(x)=x(s-2x)^2",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The square base has side $s-2x$ and the height is $x$, so $V(x)=x(s-2x)^2$ cubic units.",
          "worked": "Removing $x$ from each end leaves a square base of side $s-2x$. Folding the flaps gives height $x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}V(x)&=(s-2x)^2\\times x\\\\V(x)&=x(s-2x)^2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe volume is measured in cubic units.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p81-q54-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What is the domain of $V$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p81-q54-b-short-domain",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "0\\le x\\le\\frac{s}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", including the zero-volume limiting cases.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p81-q54-b-short-qualification",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A non-degenerate open box requires ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "0<x<\\frac{s}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For $s>0$, non-negative height and base side require\n\n$$x\\ge0,\\qquad s-2x\\ge0.$$\n\nHence the limiting-case model has domain\n\n$$0\\le x\\le\\frac{s}{2}.$$\n\nAt $x=0$ the height vanishes; at $x=\\frac{s}{2}$ the base vanishes. A non-degenerate open box instead requires $0<x<\\frac{s}{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p81-q54-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph of $V$ against $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p81-q54-c-short-shape",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "A positive hump with filled endpoints at ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(0,0)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\left(\\frac{s}{2},0\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", horizontal at the latter.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p81-q54-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use the single root ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and double root ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{s}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", restricting the sketch to the model domain.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V(x)&=x(s-2x)^2\\\\V(x)&=4x\\left(x-\\frac{s}{2}\\right)^2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere is a single root at $x=0$ and a double root at $x=\\frac{s}{2}$. For $0<x<\\frac{s}{2}$, the volume is positive.\n\nOn $0\\le x\\le\\frac{s}{2}$, the curve rises from the origin to one positive maximum, then falls to $\\left(\\frac{s}{2},0\\right)$, becoming horizontal there. Both endpoints are included.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p81-q54-c-volume-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"volumeBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"Volume function and its included endpoint markers, distinct from the black axes\"}],\"reference\":\"Answer PDF 19, printed 597, Q54(c)\"}\n\\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,draw=black,text=black,line cap=round,line join=round,>=Stealth,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,inner sep=1pt}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{volumeBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-1.4,-1.05) rectangle (4.6,4.35);\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (-1.1,0)--(4.3,0);\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-0.95)--(0,4.15);\n\\node[anchor=north,yshift=-3pt] at (4.3,0) {$x$};\n\\node[anchor=east,xshift=-3pt] at (0,4.03) {$V(x)$};\n% Normalised plotting parameter t=2x/s: X=3t and Y=40V/s^3=20t(1-t)^2.\n\\draw[volumeBlue,line width=0.8pt] plot[domain=0:1,samples=101,variable=\\t] ({3*\\t},{20*\\t*(1-\\t)^2});\n\\fill[volumeBlue] (0,0) circle[radius=1.5pt];\n\\fill[volumeBlue] (3,0) circle[radius=1.5pt];\n\\node[anchor=north,yshift=-3pt,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (3,0) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\frac{s}{2}$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 68,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 19,
                "sourceRegion": "Answer book, printed page 597, top of right column, Q54(c)",
                "description": "Restricted positive volume hump with black axes labelled x and V(x), filled blue endpoints at the origin and x=s/2, and a horizontal approach to the right endpoint. No grid, origin label or calculated maximum coordinates.",
                "mathematics": "For s>0, plot V(x)=x(s−2x)^2 only on 0≤x≤s/2. The plotting parameter t=2x/s runs from 0 to 1. Diagram coordinates are X=3t and Y=40V/s^3=20t(1−t)^2, preserving the exact function shape under positive axis scaling.",
                "answerVisibility": "Solution only. Filled endpoints implement the approved inclusive limiting-case domain."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
